WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
You've learned how to think about triage. Now for the raw material you'll actually triage.

2
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.710
Most of it comes from one tool: EDR.

3
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:16.820
EDR — Endpoint Detection and Response — is an agent installed on laptops, servers, and workstations.

4
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:26.710
It continuously records what happens on that machine: every process that runs, every file created, every network connection, every registry change.

5
00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:32.210
CrowdStrike Falcon and Microsoft Defender for Endpoint are two of the most widely deployed.

6
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:39.410
Legacy antivirus mostly matched signatures — comparing a file to a database of known-bad hashes.

7
00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:45.290
That's fast, but blind to anything new — change the malware slightly and it sails right past.

8
00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:54.460
EDR watches behavior — the sequence of actions a process takes — and keeps a rolling window of telemetry, so you can look backward in time, not just react to the moment.

9
00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.580
Whatever the vendor, the same fields recur. The process — the executable that ran.

10
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:06.580
The parent process — what launched it. This context is often what gives the whole alert away.

11
00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.040
The command line — the arguments it ran with, frequently the smoking gun.

12
00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.220
The hash — a fingerprint you can pivot on and look up in threat intel.

13
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:21.000
And severity — the vendor's confidence. A starting point, never the final verdict.

14
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:28.170
This is the trap to avoid. When EDR flags something, it generates a detection, or an alert.

15
00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:33.690
That's the vendor's claim that a pattern worth your attention matched — not proof of an attack.

16
00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:39.350
It still has to go through triage: true positive, false positive, or benign true positive.

17
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:44.770
Learn to read one vendor's alert fluently, and it transfers to the rest.

18
00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:49.520
Process, parent, command line, hash, severity — read them, then decide.
